    <string name="lore_mimic">A book chest with teeth. Eats whole books, grows from a little casket into a living bookcase.</string>
    <string name="lore_kitsune">A fox spirit. Every genre you finish grows her a new tail of its colour, nine at most.</string>
    <string name="lore_slime">A friendly jelly. After a chapter, name one thing from the book and it swallows it for good: you\'ll see it inside.</string>
    <string name="lore_dragon">Hoards finished books the way other dragons hoard gold, and sleeps on the pile.</string>
    <string name="lore_phoenix">Never turns to stone. Leave it and it burns to ash; come back and it rises brighter.</string>
    <string name="lore_griffin">Proud and quick. Loves a reading streak and spreads its wings wider with every stage.</string>
    <string name="lore_owlbear">A bear with an owl\'s face, never without a book. Turns scholarly with age: spectacles, then a mantle.</string>
    <string name="lore_moth">Comes out at night. Every night of reading adds a star to its wings.</string>
